<section>
  <h4>Features</h4>
  <p>A lightweight, privacy-first monitoring tool for WordPress sites.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Real-time status checking every 60 seconds</li>
    <li>Browser notifications on status changes</    <li>Response time tracking</li>
    <li>Status history with timestamps</li>
    <li>JSON export and import</li>
    <li>Data stored in localStorage — no server required</li>
  </ul>
</section>
<section>
  <h4>How It Works</h4>
  <p>The app uses the Fetch API with <code>no-cors</code> mode to check if your sites are reachable. Because it uses no-cors, it can only determine reachability (not HTTP status codes), but this is sufficient for uptime monitoring.</p>
  <p>All data is stored in your browser's localStorage. Nothing is sent to any server.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h4>Privacy</h4>
  <p>WordPress Monitor runs entirely in your browser. No data is sent to any external service. Site URLs and status history are stored only in localStorage and never leave your device.</p>
</section>
